## Tracker

- active: {{TRACKER_ACTIVE}}       <!-- github | local -->
- local-path: `.scratch/`
- prd-language: {{PRD_LANGUAGE}}   <!-- en | cs -->

`/to-prd` writes PRD prose (title, problem, AC text) in this language. Section headings stay English. `/implement` and `/verify` comments on the ticket use the same language.

When `active: local`, see `docs/agents/issue-tracker.local.md` (if present) for file conventions.

## UX review

- ux-review: {{UX_REVIEW}}   <!-- enabled | disabled -->

**enabled** — `/verify` Phase 2 after Functional green; hard gate on Critical/Major; after UX fixes re-run local tooling before Ship.

**disabled** — Ship right after Functional green.

## Work types

| Type | Pipeline | branch-owner typical |
|------|----------|----------------------|
| **feature** | `/align` → `/to-prd` → `/implement` → `/verify` (functional [→ ux] → ship) | agent (full-agentic) or human (human-owned) |
| **complex bug** | same as feature; `/align` if root cause unclear | agent or human |
| **simple bug** | skip `/align`; ticket with AC → `/implement` | human |
| **trivial fix** | outside pipeline — direct fix + commit | n/a |

### Bug fast-path

1. Create bug issue (GitHub with `prd` omitted, or `.scratch/prd/NNN-slug.md` with `Kind: bug`; next ID shared with `.scratch/prd/done/`) with acceptance criteria.
2. `/implement #issue` implements AC from the ticket body, then runs `/verify`. User-invoked `/implement` does not need `ready-for-agent`.

## Session override

User may pass `/implement #N human` or `/implement #N agent` to override branch-owner for one session.
